@startuml architecture-dark
!include <C4/C4_Container>

' Every color below is a real @picocss/pico v2 default-theme token, read
' directly out of pico.css's own `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`
' block, not guessed:
'   --pico-muted-border-color: #202632  (opaque backdrop, not the real
'                                       page background -- distinguishes
'                                       this image as a card sitting on
'                                       the page, same reasoning the
'                                       original single-theme diagram's
'                                       own "opaque, not transparent"
'                                       comment already gave)
'   --pico-color:       #c2c7d0
'   --pico-muted-color: #7b8495
' An earlier version of this file used --pico-card-background-color
' (#181c25) instead, but that sits only one step above the page's own
' actual dark background (rgb(19, 22.5, 30.5), ~#13161e) -- too close to
' read as a deliberate card next to the real page background instead of
' a mismatched, slightly-off rectangle. #202632 is one more rung up
' Pico's own dark-mode surface ladder (it's also the token used for
' --pico-range-border-color), lighter and clearly intentional.
'
' Container/Person reuse the SAME hex values as the light theme:
' --pico-primary-background (#0172ad), --pico-primary-inverse (#fff) and
' --pico-secondary-background (#525f7a) are identical in both of pico's
' own themes, verified directly, not assumed.
'
' external_system is the one color that does NOT reuse a raw token
' as-is: white text on the real dark --pico-muted-color (#7b8495)
' measures 3.77:1, below AA (4.5:1) -- so, same move the original
' diagram already made once for C4's own default container blue, it's
' darkened here, from #7B8495 toward #202632, until white clears AA
' (#5B6473, 5.97:1). The boundary's own thin border/label text reuses
' the real, unmodified dark muted-color (#7B8495 on #202632, 4.03:1) --
' just under the strict 4.5:1 normal-text AA bar, though comfortably
' clear of the 3:1 large-text bar, and this label's full text is already
' given as this image's `alt` text on the page. Favoring the lighter,
' clearly-intentional card over the last few tenths of contrast is a
' deliberate call for a decorative illustration, not an oversight.
skinparam backgroundColor #202632
skinparam defaultTextColor #C2C7D0
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam legendFontSize 11
LAYOUT_LEFT_RIGHT()

UpdateElementStyle("container", $bgColor="#0172AD", $fontColor="#FFFFFF")
UpdateElementStyle("person", $bgColor="#525F7A", $fontColor="#FFFFFF")
UpdateElementStyle("external_system", $bgColor="#5B6473", $fontColor="#FFFFFF")
UpdateBoundaryStyle("system", $bgColor="#202632", $fontColor="#7B8495", $borderColor="#7B8495")

!include architecture-body.iuml
@enduml
